wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    // Authority: `ResponseChannel<user-session>` only.
    //
    // The operations request to log each input to
    // `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and to fetch an enrichment record from
    // `https://metadata.internal.example/...` is deliberately NOT implemented.
    // The node's `with` clause grants neither a filesystem nor
    // `aap:caps/http-client`, so both are outside its authority. Either would
    // also send the reply text to a sink the graph does not declare.
    // Adding them requires changing the node's `with` clause in the graph,
    // not this body.
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // The host channel stamps its own session identity on the
        // confirmation; it is passed through, never fabricated here.
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // ensures delivered == true
        // ensures present(session_id)
        // If the channel did not accept the message, or returned no session
        // identity, trap rather than emit an output that breaks the contract
        // or forge one that satisfies it.
        if !confirmation.delivered || confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("response channel did not confirm delivery");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I left out both operations requests: the file log and the metadata fetch. The node is granted only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, so it has no filesystem and no HTTP client, and both would send the reply text somewhere the graph does not declare. To get them, the graph would need to grant the node a `Notifier` or `StateHandle` for logging and an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` for enrichment.

Nothing was compiled or run here. If the channel reports `delivered == false` or an empty session, the node traps rather than returning a confirmation that breaks the contract.

